WEBVTT

00:00:30.458 --> 00:00:31.708
[whirring]

00:00:38.833 --> 00:00:39.916
[ticking]

00:00:44.208 --> 00:00:45.458
ORIGINAL PATENT
Granted to Agnes De'Snake

00:00:45.541 --> 00:00:46.541
[Gary gasps]

00:00:49.583 --> 00:00:54.166
[laughs] I'm gonna burn it all
to the ground!

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:58.416
I'm a real Lynxley! [laughs]

00:00:59.875 --> 00:01:01.333
[all gasp]

00:01:01.416 --> 00:01:03.958
[panting]

00:01:04.041 --> 00:01:05.083
[all exhale]

00:01:05.666 --> 00:01:08.625
That'll do, pig. That'll do.

00:01:09.416 --> 00:01:10.958
[Moosebridge]
Astonishing news today

00:01:11.041 --> 00:01:14.375
after officers Judy Hopps
and Nicholas Wilde

00:01:14.458 --> 00:01:16.916
along with a pit viper
and a beaver

00:01:17.083 --> 00:01:19.000
foiled another
major conspiracy

00:01:19.083 --> 00:01:21.833
by revealing the true inventor
of the city's weather walls

00:01:21.916 --> 00:01:22.916
was a snake.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.000
Agnes De'Snake

00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:26.125
[Growley]
While the now
disgraced Lynxley family

00:01:26.208 --> 00:01:28.541
were revealed to have stolen
the original plans

00:01:28.625 --> 00:01:30.250
and covered it up for decades.

00:01:30.333 --> 00:01:34.125
You have not heard the last
of Milton Lyn...

00:01:34.208 --> 00:01:36.125
[Moosebridge]
Their Tundratown expansion

00:01:36.208 --> 00:01:38.958
-
now officially canceled.
-[animals cheering]

00:01:39.041 --> 00:01:41.458
[Fuzzby] Some are calling you
the dream team.

00:01:41.541 --> 00:01:42.666
How did you do it?

00:01:43.541 --> 00:01:48.625
Uh... Well, there's a lot of
different animals out there.

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:51.375
And sometimes,
we start to look

00:01:51.458 --> 00:01:54.250
at all the little reasons
that we're not the same.

00:01:55.208 --> 00:01:56.833
And it makes us worry.

00:01:58.625 --> 00:02:01.625
But maybe if
we just talked to each other,

00:02:01.708 --> 00:02:04.791
if we just tried
to understand one another,

00:02:04.875 --> 00:02:06.958
we would see
that our differences...

00:02:07.041 --> 00:02:08.166
Me - You
Sorry I fanged you -Gary

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:10.291
...don't really make
any difference at all.

00:02:10.375 --> 00:02:16.375
Maybe we'd even see that
what makes me me and you you,

00:02:16.458 --> 00:02:19.625
can make us even stronger.

00:02:20.625 --> 00:02:24.208
And with hard work, you're
gonna get to that by year two!

00:02:24.291 --> 00:02:26.000
[clapping, chattering]

00:02:26.083 --> 00:02:27.083
[whispering] Zebros.

00:02:28.166 --> 00:02:29.916
Actually, my name is Gene.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.583
[sniffles] My name...

00:02:32.208 --> 00:02:34.125
is also Gene.

00:02:34.208 --> 00:02:35.208
-Zebros!
-Zebros!

00:02:39.416 --> 00:02:40.958
[bunny children laughing]

00:02:41.041 --> 00:02:42.041
[bunny children exclaim]

00:02:42.916 --> 00:02:44.041
He did it!

00:02:44.125 --> 00:02:45.416
[laughter]

00:02:46.333 --> 00:02:47.708
Kids, get off the snake.

00:02:47.791 --> 00:02:50.291
-[bunnies giggling]
-[Clawhauser gasps] Aw!

00:02:51.791 --> 00:02:53.583
-Hi. How is everybody doing?
-[knocking]

00:02:53.666 --> 00:02:55.333
[gasps] Oh!
[stammers] One sec!

00:02:57.166 --> 00:02:59.208
[exclaiming]

00:03:00.416 --> 00:03:01.625
[Gary chuckles]

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:09.041
This is my family.

00:03:09.666 --> 00:03:11.125
Permission to hug?

00:03:15.958 --> 00:03:17.083
Thank you.

00:03:17.166 --> 00:03:19.125
[chuckling]

00:03:19.208 --> 00:03:21.291
[♪ gentle music playing]

00:03:21.375 --> 00:03:24.083
Hey, uh, I got you something.

00:03:29.125 --> 00:03:30.541
-[gasps]
-[Nick chuckles]

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.500
Love you, partner.

00:03:34.583 --> 00:03:37.833
But I am still me, so I'm
only saying it once a decade.

00:03:38.375 --> 00:03:40.291
[Nick, through carrot pen]
Love you, partner.

00:03:40.375 --> 00:03:41.416
Oh, I'm gonna need that back.

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:44.416
I'll give it back to you
after our next case.

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:46.250
There's gonna be
another case, huh?

00:03:46.333 --> 00:03:48.500
Of course. Because,
when you broke out of jail,

00:03:48.583 --> 00:03:51.166
you also released 200
highly dangerous prisoners.

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:52.625
Worth it.

00:03:52.708 --> 00:03:54.541
Any idea
where you want to start?

00:03:54.625 --> 00:03:55.708
[Judy chuckles]

00:03:55.791 --> 00:03:57.791
[♪ "Down Under" playing]

00:04:00.625 --> 00:04:02.583
Oh. Mmm. Mmm.

00:04:02.666 --> 00:04:05.625
One-way ticket
to Outback Island, please.

00:04:05.708 --> 00:04:06.708
First class.

00:04:06.791 --> 00:04:08.583
[Australian accent] Very nice.

00:04:08.666 --> 00:04:11.208
Oh, and remember, if you're
happy with our service,

00:04:11.291 --> 00:04:14.708
please be sure to leave us
four thumbs up.

00:04:14.791 --> 00:04:16.625
Oh, I will.

00:04:16.708 --> 00:04:18.375
[sighs]

00:04:18.458 --> 00:04:20.375
[slurps, exhales deeply]

00:04:22.375 --> 00:04:23.458
Hopps and Wilde?

00:04:23.541 --> 00:04:26.250
Wilde and Cabbagepatch.

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:31.041
